00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:25.830
Time to go?

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:30.430
Yeah. Well then, Mum, we're heading home.

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:33.690
So this is only the third time we've visited her grave.

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:37.560
Even though it's the anniversary of Mum's death today, we miss it nearly every year.

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:40.760
It's okay, we came to see her at least.

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:46.850
It's better to not have gatherings filled with people who don't care.

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:51.450
That's true.

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:54.780
Let's go.

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:56.600
What is it?

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:58.120
It's okay once in a while, right?

00:02:58.120 --> 00:02:59.280
No, it's not!

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:01.890
You're blushing.

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:06.490
Last time, you wouldn't go anywhere unless I held your hand and dragged you along.

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:08.880
That's when we were kids!

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:13.800
Yeah, it's certainly something in the past when we were kids.

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:20.800
It's been a while and I guess those past feelings came back when I was talking to Mum.

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:47.610
This is just too little after ending my maigre days.

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:50.510
You're the one who decided on this place.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:54.700
Ending your maigre days? Stop talking like an old man.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:58.190
I'm not acting like an old man. It's called having a rich vocabulary.

00:03:58.190 --> 00:04:00.400
In other words, being an adult.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:02.290
What is it?

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:05.000
Don't act high and mighty when you have food on your face.

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:06.750
Here.

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:09.970
See?

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:12.640
You're such a child.

00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:16.730
Thank you very much.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:18.890
It's gotten a bit late.

00:04:18.890 --> 00:04:20.550
Does it matter?

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:23.680
Yeah. That house...

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:27.820
Going back early is just a constraint.

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:38.470
What is it? You're acting weird.

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:46.540
Hey, that shop is open even at this time.

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:48.430
Wanna go in and have a look?

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:49.760
Sure, I guess.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:52.520
<b>F
a
n
c
y

00:04:53.990 --> 00:04:55.980
This is so cute too.

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:59.370
Window shopping is fun too.

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:00.570
Really?

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:02.490
That looks pretty good too.

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:06.490
So these are called Misangas.

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:09.490
So many different patterns.

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:12.390
I'll buy it for you if you like it.

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:19.340
Well, it's just that a lot has happened lately, and you've been kinda depressed.

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:22.010
So, how do I put it...?

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:25.550
So, you want to get me a present to cheer me up?

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:27.710
Yeah. Something like that.

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:30.240
How generous.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:35.160
Okay, I guess I'll buy one too.

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:37.090
I said that I'll get you one if you want it.

00:05:37.090 --> 00:05:40.360
I know. The one I'm buying is for you.

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:42.710
For me?

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:43.720
Yep.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:51.370
I know you're going through the same pain as I am.

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:53.790
Sis...

00:05:54.110 --> 00:05:57.200
So, let me buy a present for you too.

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:08.970
It's been a while since we've worn a matching pair, hasn't it?

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:26.250
<b>Principal's Office</b>

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:26.820
What's the meaning of this?

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:29.210
Shuusuke and I in a love hotel?

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:31.100
Who would say such a thing?

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:32.850
We don't know who it's from.

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:38.550
However, it was written in an anonymous letter we received yesterday.

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:45.180
Sakuranomori High School

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:45.180
Principal

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:45.180
It alleges that you two were seen entering a suspicious place last Saturday night.

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:50.560
But, Shuusuke and I are siblings.

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:52.720
Thus the problem.

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:57.730
Of course, even if you weren't, it'd still be a problem.

00:06:58.470 --> 00:07:02.420
Either way, there's no truth in those allegations. It must be some mistake!

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:08.680
Then where and what were the two of you doing last Saturday night?

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:12.590
We were grave visiting.

00:07:12.590 --> 00:07:15.400
Grave visiting? During this season?

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:21.210
That day was the death anniversary of our real mother.

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:27.720
After the visit, we had dinner together, went to a fancy shop, then went home.

00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:32.140
Do you have anyone who can prove it?

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:34.620
Proof?

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:35.960
You don't, do you?

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:38.530
Perhaps one of the workers at the shops.

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:41.020
Perhaps, you say?

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:42.860
Hold it right there!

00:07:42.860 --> 00:07:47.600
You're doubting the students because of an anonymous letter you received?

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:50.280
The letter could be a prank.

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:55.290
Then, do you know anyone who would pull this kind of prank?

00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:57.210
No.

00:07:57.950 --> 00:08:02.500
I see. In that case, this letter has credibility.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:04.890
Stop twisting the facts!

00:08:04.890 --> 00:08:11.190
Fujimura-sensei, I understand how you feel. But aren't you siding with the students too much?

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:15.840
Vice principal, I'm their homeroom teacher!

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:18.970
How could I call myself their teacher if I don't side with them?

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:21.220
That's true but...

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:22.510
Wakatsuki-san.

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:29.450
Sakuranomori High School

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:29.450
Principal

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:27.710
Certainly, I have my suspicions about the letter we received as well.

00:08:27.710 --> 00:08:30.510
The contents seem difficult to palate.

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:36.310
Thus the school will not pursue this matter any further.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:44.730
However, we must report to your parents that the school received such a letter.

00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:46.480
No way...

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:47.810
Understood?

00:08:49.010 --> 00:08:52.180
As expected, you make very wise decisions, principal.

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:03.270
Shuusuke!

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:05.240
That's horrible!

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:09.650
What have you done?! Do you understand the importance of this period?

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:13.940
I can't have this happen with the approval so close.

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:17.430
If this were to leak, do you know the damage it would cause?

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:19.040
What the hell did you say?!
-Don't!

00:09:21.020 --> 00:09:26.590
Why? What should I do? Why at a time like this?

00:09:30.820 --> 00:09:32.150
...is how it is.

00:09:32.150 --> 00:09:33.720
What are you saying?

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:36.980
Oh, sorry!

00:09:36.980 --> 00:09:39.150
The insides are still rattling.

00:09:39.150 --> 00:09:40.430
Are you all right?

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:42.830
But, who did this to you?

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:44.900
Just to let you know, it wasn't me...

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:55.750
Shuri!

00:09:56.810 --> 00:09:59.290
Wait, Shuri!

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:04.500
<b>S
h
u
r
i</b>

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:04.500
<b>S
h
u
u
s
u
k
e</b>

00:10:06.060 --> 00:10:07.800
Who wrote this?

00:10:09.050 --> 00:10:12.170
I'm asking who the fuck wrote this!

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:14.840
Shuu.

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:17.330
If I don't get an answer, I'm gonna beat the shit outta all of you!

00:10:17.330 --> 00:10:18.660
Stop it, Shuu.

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:22.160
Shut the hell up! I won't allow anyone to hurt my sister!

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:23.310
Stay calm.

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:25.510
Let go of me. I said let go!

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:28.320
God damnit!

00:10:44.010 --> 00:10:46.950
I see, so that's what happened.

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:49.250
I'm sorry to scare you like that this morning.

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:51.920
Not at all, it wasn't your fault.

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:54.720
Yeah. Who would write such a letter?

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:58.450
I don't know. The sender was anonymous.

00:10:58.450 --> 00:11:01.990
The contents were written with a word processor, so no leads came to mind.

00:11:01.990 --> 00:11:06.550
The teachers are crazy for believing such a dodgy letter.

00:11:06.550 --> 00:11:09.400
Yuzuki-sensei was sticking up for us though.

00:11:09.400 --> 00:11:11.150
But the vice principal...

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:15.780
The school contacted our house, and some chaos ensued because of that.

00:11:16.250 --> 00:11:20.070
Is it a bad idea asking you to come visiting with us at a time like this?

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:24.810
It's okay. It's a change of pace. I'm grateful actually.

00:11:24.810 --> 00:11:28.630
Also, I don't really want to go back home.

00:11:30.140 --> 00:11:33.870
By the way, is Kaji-san okay since she had to be hospitalised?

00:11:33.870 --> 00:11:37.550
I heard that her cold got worse and it became pneumonia.

00:11:38.150 --> 00:11:43.480
She's practically recovered already though. But, they're keeping her in for observation just in case.

00:11:43.900 --> 00:11:46.240
Then, let's cheer her up.

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:47.640
Yep, that's right.

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:52.090
Come in.

00:11:52.640 --> 00:11:55.540
Pardon us. We came to visit.

00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:57.700
Oh my, you...

00:11:57.700 --> 00:12:00.950
Dear me, all of you came.

00:12:01.790 --> 00:12:03.680
Is it okay for you to be up?

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:05.560
Yes, I'm all better now.

00:12:05.560 --> 00:12:08.880
I see. Here's a gift for you.

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:11.080
Thank you.

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:13.610
Do you have a small knife?

00:12:13.610 --> 00:12:18.310
Yeah. Inside those drawers. There's a cutting board and plates too.

00:12:18.310 --> 00:12:20.700
I'll peel it then, okay?

00:12:21.660 --> 00:12:27.510
Hey, I may be a klutz, but I can at least peel apples.

00:12:33.070 --> 00:12:35.860
See, they're peeled nicely, aren't they?

00:12:36.340 --> 00:12:38.960
I can do it if I try.

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:40.290
That's right.

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:42.550
Maybe I should carve little rabbits.

00:12:44.340 --> 00:12:45.810
I cut my finger.

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:49.130
Oh no, you're bleeding.

00:12:49.130 --> 00:12:51.670
Oh my, what should we do?

00:12:51.890 --> 00:12:53.860
I'm okay. It's nothing.

00:12:53.860 --> 00:12:57.820
I'll grab a band-aid, but before that some antiseptic.

00:12:58.370 --> 00:13:01.130
You don't have to get so worked up.

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:02.880
Let's clean that under the tap.

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:04.670
I just have to suck on it a bit.

00:13:04.670 --> 00:13:06.190
Hurry.

00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:19.860
Good as new.

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:21.650
Thank you.

00:13:24.180 --> 00:13:27.720
What's wrong? Your face is all blue.

00:13:28.590 --> 00:13:31.490
Nothing's wrong...

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:33.650
Really... nothing...

00:13:33.650 --> 00:13:35.590
Nothing? You don't look okay...

00:13:35.590 --> 00:13:37.610
Sorry, I'm going to the restroom.

00:13:37.610 --> 00:13:39.540
Hey! 
-Hidaka-kun?

00:14:06.870 --> 00:14:09.120
I wonder what's wrong with him.

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:11.370
That wasn't normal.

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:13.720
I'm going to go check up on him.

00:14:16.430 --> 00:14:21.090
Sorry, we came to visit you, but we're just making a commotion.

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:24.010
Say, Wakatsuki-san?

00:14:24.670 --> 00:14:30.310
I've told you about the legend of the Twin Hills before, haven't I?

00:14:30.690 --> 00:14:36.810
Yeah. You said that wishes would come true if the sakuras on both hills bloomed, right?

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:42.520
Yes. Because of that, they offered sacrifices in the past.

00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:48.130
But, that was truly a long time ago. During the Edo period they switched to the sakura dance.

00:14:48.130 --> 00:14:53.100
I made a wish to the sakuras of the Twin Hills.

00:14:53.100 --> 00:14:57.970
I wished for Motoko... my granddaughter Motoko to be returned to me.

00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:05.560
She was so cute, kind and good with the violin.

00:15:05.560 --> 00:15:09.930
There wasn't a single reason for her to die before me.

00:15:10.850 --> 00:15:14.030
But, she got involved in that accident!

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:18.300
It must have been a mistake for her to lose her life.

00:15:18.300 --> 00:15:21.710
It's definitely a mistake!

00:15:21.710 --> 00:15:25.430
I had to do something to let this terrible mistake be known.

00:15:25.430 --> 00:15:29.210
That's why I made a prayer to the sakuras of the Twin Hills.

00:15:29.210 --> 00:15:35.050
I asked them to resurrect her. 
I asked them to return her to me.

00:15:37.030 --> 00:15:42.870
The sakura season came, but the sakuras on the elder sister hill never bloomed.

00:15:43.190 --> 00:15:49.680
Surely, they'll not grant wishes without some form of payment. I was too self-centred.

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:56.480
That's why, I offered sacrifices to the non-blooming sakuras of the elder sister hill.

00:15:56.480 --> 00:15:59.980
First was a little bird. Next was a cat.

00:16:03.710 --> 00:16:05.180
No way...

00:16:05.180 --> 00:16:11.760
I tried so many things, but the sakuras wouldn't bloom no matter how much time passed.

00:16:11.760 --> 00:16:15.160
I guess it has to be a person.

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:18.150
What are you saying?

00:16:18.150 --> 00:16:19.900
Forgive me.

00:16:19.900 --> 00:16:24.270
I feel bad for you, but I don't have any other options.

00:16:24.270 --> 00:16:27.030
I'm truly sorry.

00:16:31.310 --> 00:16:35.220
Hidaka-kun is fine now. He was just feeling a little dizzy.

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:37.650
Shuri!

00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:45.980
Stop!

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:07.710
<b>In Surgery</b>

00:17:08.520 --> 00:17:10.820
How's Asami? How's my daughter?!

00:17:10.820 --> 00:17:13.180
She's doing well. There's no need to worry.

00:17:16.290 --> 00:17:19.380
Thank you so much, doctor!

00:17:25.360 --> 00:17:26.460
I'm home.

00:17:31.060 --> 00:17:34.050
Why London?

00:17:34.050 --> 00:17:35.150
Overseas study.

00:17:35.150 --> 00:17:36.670
Why so suddenly?

00:17:36.670 --> 00:17:39.890
I got you accepted into a public boarding school.

00:17:39.890 --> 00:17:43.480
You'll go when the paper work is done. Okay?

00:17:43.480 --> 00:17:46.650
No, it's not! Why do I have to study abroad?

00:17:46.650 --> 00:17:49.970
If you consider what happened, this time, it'll be a police case.

00:17:49.970 --> 00:17:52.820
What would happen if the mass media were to get wind of this?

00:17:52.820 --> 00:17:54.660
Police case?

00:17:54.660 --> 00:17:58.750
It's true that they questioned witnesses. But that was all.

00:17:58.750 --> 00:18:00.640
That's more than plenty.

00:18:00.640 --> 00:18:02.940
I was merely a victim.

00:18:02.940 --> 00:18:04.270
Perhaps.

00:18:04.690 --> 00:18:07.080
No, you definitely are.

00:18:07.080 --> 00:18:09.790
But, society won't think the same way.

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:12.870
Listen, this is for your own good.

00:18:12.870 --> 00:18:17.470
If the mass media found out, they'll spread all sorts of lies about you.

00:18:17.470 --> 00:18:19.730
They'll accuse you of things that you've never done.

00:18:19.730 --> 00:18:22.670
I don't want those kinda things to happen to you.

00:18:22.670 --> 00:18:24.650
You should go somewhere where they can't...

00:18:24.650 --> 00:18:26.310
Quit running my life for me!

00:18:26.310 --> 00:18:28.650
All you think about is your damn election!

00:18:29.660 --> 00:18:33.850
Certainly, you'd be in a bad position if this were to leak out since the elections are so close.

00:18:33.850 --> 00:18:35.180
No, I just...

00:18:35.180 --> 00:18:39.000
There have been rumours circulating about the new town hall involving money.

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:42.870
So, to prevent any more problems, you're getting rid of me, right?!

00:18:42.870 --> 00:18:44.200
Shuri!

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:47.470
I definitely won't go to London!

00:18:55.330 --> 00:18:58.570
Sis, what's wrong? Did something happen?

00:18:59.790 --> 00:19:00.760
Sis.

00:19:01.400 --> 00:19:02.830
Sis, I'm coming in.

00:19:08.900 --> 00:19:13.130
Sis, he didn't hit you again, did he?

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:17.140
Then, what happened?

00:19:17.140 --> 00:19:18.290
Shuusuke!

00:19:18.930 --> 00:19:21.640
Asami... Asami got hurt.

00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:24.630
Hoshino-san? How?

00:19:24.630 --> 00:19:27.720
She protected me.

00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:31.110
Then, there was so much blood...

00:19:34.800 --> 00:19:37.610
I see. So that's what happened.

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:41.240
But, why do you have to go to London?

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:45.470
I don't want to go. But, with all that's happened to us... I'm sure...

00:19:45.470 --> 00:19:48.460
What are you saying? I'll object too.

00:19:48.460 --> 00:19:51.500
I won't let him get his way...

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:54.300
It's the same when that woman came into our lives.

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:58.900
No matter how much we objected, he said that it was already prearranged.

00:19:58.900 --> 00:20:01.660
And it was over...

00:20:03.230 --> 00:20:04.790
I don't want to go!

00:20:04.790 --> 00:20:09.480
I've already lost Mum. Now I have to be separated from you.

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:12.930
I won't be able to take it.

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:14.910
Sis...

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:18.500
How long will this continue?

00:20:18.500 --> 00:20:22.820
How long are we gonna let that bastard control us?

00:20:33.820 --> 00:20:34.970
Sis.

00:20:38.230 --> 00:20:42.470
If you don't want to be separated from me, then let's go together.

00:20:43.710 --> 00:20:46.700
Far away, to where his hands can't reach.

00:20:46.700 --> 00:20:47.760
But...

00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:49.830
It's okay.

00:20:50.150 --> 00:20:53.280
If you're worried, or scared, or hesitant...

00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:57.230
...then this time, I'll be the one pulling your hand.

00:21:00.040 --> 00:21:01.330
Shuusuke.

00:21:25.540 --> 00:21:28.950
Shuusuke, do you remember the day when Sana transferred here?

00:21:28.950 --> 00:21:32.120
I do. That slap on the face sure was effective!

00:21:32.120 --> 00:21:36.310
The BBQ by the river, playing at the spa; it sure was fun.

00:21:36.310 --> 00:21:39.990
Then, Nanaka's sakura dance at the festival was so beautiful too.

00:21:39.990 --> 00:21:42.520
The hero show at the theme park was exciting too.

00:21:42.930 --> 00:21:46.840
But those fun days aren't coming back, are they?

00:21:47.670 --> 00:21:51.300
Next time on Myself; Yourself: Confession

00:21:49.250 --> 00:21:55.030
Confession

00:21:51.760 --> 00:21:54.850
Why, why did it become like this?
